      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): bridge presentation capabilities and renderPresentation through channel outbound facade",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSlack channel outbound facade does not bridge `renderPresentation` to the core delivery pipeline. Slack replies always render as fallback plain text instead of using the presentation capabilities configured for the agent (e.g., rich formatting, interactive cards).\n\nCloses #95440\n\n## Fix\n\nBridge `renderPresentation` through the Slack channel outbound facade so Slack replies respect the agent presentation configuration.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Slack proof — presentation delivers card receipt\n\n```\npnpm openclaw message send --channel slack \\\n  --target \"channel:随机\" \\\n  --message \"95463 Proof — Block Kit\" \\\n  --presentation '{\"title\":\"PR Proof\",\"blocks\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Block Kit ✅\"},{\"type\":\"divider\"}]}' \\\n  --json\n\n→ receipt.parts[0].kind = \"card\" ✅\n```\n\n### Slack facade presentation tests\n\n```\npnpm test extensions/slack/src/channel.test.ts\n  slackChannelOutbound presentation\n    ✓ exposes renderPresentation on the channel outbound adapter\n    ✓ exposes presentationCapabilities on the channel outbound adapter\n    ✓ delegates renderPresentation to slackOutbound and returns presentationBlocks\n  46 tests passed (1 file)\n```\n\n### Outbound-bridge receipt regression tests\n\n```\npnpm test src/channels/message/outbound-bridge.test.ts\n  createChannelMessageAdapterFromOutbound\n    ✓ infers receipt kind as card when both text and presentation are present (#95440)\n    ✓ returns text kind for payloads with only text and no presentation\n  10 tests passed (1 file)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n- [x] Bug fix\n## Scope\n- [x] Slack channel (outbound facade)\n## Security Impact\n- New permissions? No · Secrets changed? No · New network calls? No\n",
